13
00:00:31,046 --> 00:00:32,857
Therefore, you have to be specific about the

14
00:00:32,906 --> 00:00:35,535
constraints. We just added some basic

15
00:00:35,535 --> 00:00:37,106
constraint in the instructions now,

16
00:00:37,715 --> 00:00:39,943
but the more explicit you are about what

17
00:00:39,943 --> 00:00:42,332
Claude can create, what it must not touch,

18
00:00:42,524 --> 00:00:44,641
about your format requirements, about naming

19
00:00:44,673 --> 00:00:47,045
conventions, the better your results are.

20
00:00:47,895 --> 00:00:50,107
You can also make sure that Claude always

21
00:00:50,364 --> 00:00:53,282
asks questions in case anything is unclear.

22
00:00:53,490 --> 00:00:55,670
These are also things you can implement and

23
00:00:55,670 --> 00:00:57,818
we'll also learn other ways how to implement

24
00:00:57,818 --> 00:01:00,287
these in addition to the global instructions

25
00:01:00,383 --> 00:01:03,109
we saw already. To give you a better idea of

26
00:01:03,109 --> 00:01:05,771
this outcome-first approach, so you don't

27
00:01:05,771 --> 00:01:09,090
tell Cowork exactly each step it has to do,

